-- Regression proof: a module-scope TABLE constant read by a module function
-- must not be dropped while that function is spliced into this program.
--
-- `spliceReqModules` absorbs a plain-Duo `req` module into the direct
-- backend's own object, and it splices the functions the program calls. It
-- carried only LITERAL-valued bindings across, and a table literal is not one,
-- so `pick()` arrived and `slots` did not. The splice rewrites the AST the C
-- emitter walks too, so the C backend inherited the same half: twenty
-- `error: use of undeclared identifier` on `std.wasm.opcodes`, which is this
-- program's shape at full size.
--
-- Verified BY VALUE. `slots[3]` is 42 and nothing else; a build that merely
-- compiles proves nothing here, because the failure this guards against IS a
-- compile error and would flip back to green the moment the splice silently
-- stopped happening for an unrelated reason.
p = req "splicetableprobe"
os = req "std.os"

main(): i64
  v: i64 = p.pick(3)
  if v != 42
    print("req splice table constant: got {v}, want 42")
    os.exit(1)
  end
  print("req splice table constant: OK")
  0
end
